 "result_text": "`notification.add` and `notification.update` should now send a proper JSON body. I haven't run the tests or made a real API call, so the fix is unverified.\n\n**Cause:** `RachioObject._request` in `rachiopy/rachioobject.py` passed the payload with `data=body`. With a dict, `requests` form-encodes it, so the server received `device=...` instead of JSON. That's why it complained about the unrecognized token `device`.\n\n**Fix:** I changed it to `json=body`, so the dict is serialized as JSON.\n\n**Scope:** The change is in the shared `_request`, so it also affects every other `put_request` and `post_request` call (zones, devices, schedule rules). `get_request` passes no body, so it is unaffected. Any test that asserts on `data=` will need to expect `json=` instead. I didn't touch the tests, as you asked.",
